# Jak 1: the fisherman's game from the game's camera, by the hand (LIST-0.1.9 item 20; a tester: "will vr fishing be in
# next update"). Run with Fishing game in first person off (sim cfg gkcfg-fishtp; tests/jak1_fishing_eyes.sim is the game
# from his eyes) and JAKVR_TEST_CONTINUE=jungle-start JAKVR_TEST_WARP=fisher JAKVR_TEST_RIDE=1 QUEST_SIM_ALIGN=10000
# JAKVR_STATE_TRACE=1: a new game (as jak1_tether_rock.sim), the continue, Jak put by the fisherman (frame 10000), and 3
# seconds on his game starts as his question's Yes does (pc-vr.gc, fisher.gc idle: "[vr] test: the fishing game
# started"). It is seen from the game's camera (target-fishing). The right hand then held 35 cm left of the head, 35 cm
# right, in front of it (the net there, at no more than the original's speed), then the stick (the stick's net, the hand
# ignored), the stick let go (the net stays where the stick left it), the hand moved (it takes the net back), and the
# left hand raised and moved left (the raised hand has the net). Each step about a second and a half, all inside the
# game's first 15 s: missed fish lose it some 17 s in (sim s14 fi).
